From: AltarsCN <337293323+Altars3668@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 29 Sep 2026 22:05:44 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] ole32: Draw an enhanced metafile the data cache holds.

The cache loads an enhanced metafile presentation -- an OlePres stream
of CF_ENHMETAFILE keeps it as a Windows metafile, which the cache turns
back into an enhanced one -- but IViewObject::Draw() only knew metafile
pictures and DIBs, so OleDraw() of such an object answered OLE_E_BLANK,
and an embedded object that is not running, whose last picture is what
its container shows, drew nothing.  It now plays the metafile into the
bounds, which is what ole32's tests expect from Windows.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>

diff --git a/dlls/ole32/datacache.c b/dlls/ole32/datacache.c
index 0a7aaf1a7cf..2c0d8d1c513 100644
--- a/dlls/ole32/datacache.c
+++ b/dlls/ole32/datacache.c
@@ -2116,6 +2116,17 @@ static HRESULT WINAPI DataCache_Draw(
 
         return S_OK;
       }
+      case CF_ENHMETAFILE:
+      {
+          RECT rect;
+
+          if (cache_entry->stgmedium.tymed != TYMED_ENHMF)
+              continue;
+
+          SetRect( &rect, lprcBounds->left, lprcBounds->top, lprcBounds->right, lprcBounds->bottom );
+          PlayEnhMetaFile( hdcDraw, cache_entry->stgmedium.hEnhMetaFile, &rect );
+          return S_OK;
+      }
       case CF_DIB:
       {
           BITMAPINFO *info;
diff --git a/dlls/ole32/tests/ole2.c b/dlls/ole32/tests/ole2.c
index 41c8588f930..6bfcc1fbb92 100644
--- a/dlls/ole32/tests/ole2.c
+++ b/dlls/ole32/tests/ole2.c
@@ -1234,7 +1234,6 @@ static void test_OleLoad(IStorage *pStorage)
             if (fmt == CF_METAFILEPICT)
                 ok(hr == S_OK, "OleDraw error %#lx: cfFormat = %lu, advf = %#lx\n", hr, fmt, header.advf);
             else if (fmt == CF_ENHMETAFILE)
-                todo_wine
                 ok(hr == S_OK, "OleDraw error %#lx: cfFormat = %lu, advf = %#lx\n", hr, fmt, header.advf);
             else
                 ok(hr == OLE_E_BLANK || hr == OLE_E_NOTRUNNING || hr == E_FAIL, "OleDraw should fail: %#lx, cfFormat = %lu, advf = %#lx\n", hr, fmt, header.advf);
